<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Madho Singh of Kota</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1648</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Rao Madho Singh</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Madho Singh was the first ruler of Kota State in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputana">Rajputana</a>, reigning from 1631 to 1648. A son of Rao <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ratan-singh-of-bundi">Ratan Singh of Bundi</a>, he received Kota as a separate principality from the Mughal emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shah-jahan">Shah Jahan</a> as a reward for military service. His Hada <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> descendants ruled Kota until it joined the United State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a> in 1948.</p></div>
